          <h1 id="refund-title">Refund &amp; Returns Policy</h1>
          <p class="lead">This policy explains JOOD process for returns, cancellations, refunds, exchanges and warranty claims. It aims to be fair to customers while protecting contractual and operational obligations with suppliers and couriers.</p>
          <p class="muted-small"><strong>Effective date:</strong> 1 January 2026</p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-media" aria-hidden="true">
          <img src="/customer/images/return-policy/return-policy.png" alt="Returns and refunds illustration">
        </div>
      </div>
    </header>

    <!-- POLICY CONTENT -->
    <section aria-label="Refund policy content">
      <div class="grid">
        <!-- Main column -->
        <div>
          <article class="card" aria-labelledby="policy-heading">
            <h2 id="policy-heading">Purpose &amp; Scope</h2>
            <p class="muted">This Refund &amp; Returns Policy applies to purchases made through JOOD official website and other official sales channels. It describes eligibility, timelines, costs and the process to request returns, refunds or exchanges. For product-specific warranty or service terms, check the product page and warranty documentation.</p>

            <h3 id="eligibility">Eligibility for returns and refunds</h3>
            <p class="muted">An item is eligible for return or refund when:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted" aria-labelledby="eligibility">
              <li>The request is submitted within the stated return window (standard: <strong>14 calendar days</strong> from delivery), unless the product page states otherwise.</li>
              <li>The item is substantially in the same condition as delivered — unused (unless faulty) — with original packaging, tags and accessories.</li>
              <li>Proof of purchase (order number or invoice) is provided when requested.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="non-eligible">Non-returnable items</h3>
            <p class="muted">Certain items are not eligible for return unless faulty. Typical exceptions include perishable goods (food, flowers), personalised items, sealed hygiene products once opened, digital downloads and items explicitly marked 'final sale'. Always review product-specific return notes before purchasing.</p>

            <h3 id="timeframes">Timeframes &amp; statutory rights</h3>
            <p class="muted">Our standard return window is <strong>14 calendar days</strong> from the date of delivery for most consumer goods. For warranty claims, refer to the manufacturer warranty period described on the product page. If local law provides stronger consumer rights (longer return period, etc.), we will comply with that local law.</p>

            <h3 id="how-to-return">How to initiate a return or claim</h3>
            <ol class="value-list muted" aria-labelledby="how-to-return">
              <li>Sign in to your account → My Orders → Select the order and click "Request Return".</li>
              <li>Or, open a support ticket via <a href="/customer/contact-us">Contact Us</a> with your order number, photos, and a description.</li>
              <li>Choose your preferred remedy — refund, exchange, or store credit (if available).</li>
              <li>Follow the instructions to print a prepaid label or to schedule a carrier pickup where offered.</li>
              <li>Pack items securely with all original documentation and keep proof of postage/tracking until the refund is processed.</li>
            </ol>

            <h3 id="inspection">Inspection &amp; outcomes</h3>
            <p class="muted">Returned items are inspected on receipt. If the item meets return conditions we will process the requested remedy. If it fails inspection (e.g., used beyond inspection, missing components, or intentional damage), we may:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Refuse the return and return the item to you (at your expense),</li>
              <li>Offer a partial refund to reflect diminished value, or</li>
              <li>Apply a restocking fee where explicitly stated in product terms.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="refund-processing">Refund method &amp; processing times</h3>
            <p class="muted">Refunds are normally issued to the original payment method unless otherwise agreed. Typical timelines after the refund is issued by us:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Card refunds: usually 5–10 business days (subject to card issuer/bank).</li>
              <li>Bank transfers: typically 5–10 business days depending on banking partners.</li>
              <li>Store credit / wallet: usually within 3 business days.</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="muted">We’ll email you once the refund is processed. Actual bank posting times are outside our control.</p>

            <h3 id="faulty">Faulty, damaged or incorrect items</h3>
            <p class="muted">If you receive an item that is faulty, damaged or incorrect:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Contact support immediately with photos/videos and your order number.</li>
              <li>We will assess and — where appropriate — provide a replacement, repair, or full refund and arrange collection at our cost.</li>
              <li>For manufacturer-covered faults, we will coordinate with the manufacturer as necessary.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="shipping-costs">Return shipping costs</h3>
            <p class="muted">Who pays depends on the reason for return:</p>
            <ul class="value-list muted">
              <li>Our error (damaged, incorrect, or faulty): we cover return shipping/collection costs.</li>
              <li>Change of mind: the customer pays return postage unless a free returns program is offered.</li>
              <li>International returns: customers are generally responsible for return shipping, duties and taxes unless otherwise agreed.</li>
            </ul>

            <h3 id="restocking">Restocking fees &amp; deductions</h3>
            <p class="muted">We generally do not charge restocking fees. Deductions may apply if items are returned in a condition that prevents resale. Any deduction will be explained and itemised in writing prior to finalising the refund.</p>

            <h3 id="exchanges">Exchanges &amp; replacements</h3>
            <p class="muted">If you request an exchange (size, colour, or model), we will ship a replacement subject to stock availability. If unavailable, you may choose a refund or store credit. Exchange shipping costs may apply depending on the reason for exchange.</p>

            <h3 id="international-orders">International orders &amp; customs</h3>
            <p class="muted">International customers are responsible for import duties, taxes and customs clearance unless otherwise stated. For returns from outside the UAE, follow the authorised return instructions from our support team to minimise customs complications.</p>

            <h3 id="cancellations">Order cancellations</h3>
            <p class="muted">Orders can be cancelled before dispatch. If you request cancellation after dispatch, treat the shipment as a return on receipt. Refunds for cancellations are processed once cancellation is confirmed and are subject to payment processor timelines.</p>

            <h3 id="consumer-rights">Statutory rights &amp; disputes</h3>
            <p class="muted">This policy complements your statutory consumer rights. Where local law provides greater protection, that law will apply. For unresolved disputes, customers may use the consumer dispute resolution mechanisms in their jurisdiction.</p>

            <h3 id="chargebacks">Chargebacks</h3>
            <p class="muted">If you open a payment dispute (chargeback) with your bank, please tell us. We will cooperate with the card issuer and provide evidence. Unwarranted chargebacks may require us to defend the transaction and may delay refunds until the dispute is closed.</p>

            <h3 id="privacy">Personal data</h3>
            <p class="muted">We process personal data supplied during returns and refunds only to complete the request. See our <a href="/customer/legal-and-compliance/privacy-policy">Privacy Policy</a> for retention details and rights.</p>

            <h3 id="changes">Changes to this policy</h3>
            <p class="muted">We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be posted with an updated effective date. Continued use of the service after publication constitutes acceptance of the updated policy.</p>

            <h2 id="contact">Contact &amp; support</h2>
            <p class="muted">For help with returns, refunds or warranty claims, contact our Returns Team. Provide your order number and clear photos where relevant to speed up processing.</p>

            <div class="muted" style="margin-top:10px;">
              <p><strong>Support email:</strong> <a href="mailto:support@jood.com">support@jood.com</a></p>
              <p><strong>Phone:</strong> +971-55-555-5555</p>
              <p><strong>Postal address:</strong> 13th Floor, Al Reem Tower, Dubai, UAE</p>
            </div>

            <p class="note">This policy provides operational guidance and is not legal advice. For contract-level queries, bulk purchases, or complex warranty disputes seek independent legal advice or contact our corporate team.</p>
          </article>
        </div>

        <!-- SIDEBAR -->
        <aside>
          <div class="card" role="complementary" aria-labelledby="returns-quicklinks">
